[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "Exchange Variation"]
[ECO "D36"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "minority-attack,carlsbad-structure"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "4.cxd5"]
[Start "orthodox 2...e6"]

3. Nc3 ( 3. cxd5 exd5 4. Nc3 ( 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Nc3 Be7 ) ( 4. e3 Nf6 5. Nc3 c6 ) ( 4. Bf4 Nf6 5. e3 c6 6. Nc3 Bf5 ) 4... Nf6 { Same position as after 4.cxd5 exd5 below. Black recaptures with the e-pawn, which keeps a pawn in the centre and the c8 bishop free. } ) 3... Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 ( 5. Bf4 c6 6. e3 Bf5 { The bishop comes out before the pawn on e6 is gone; Black wants it outside the pawn chain, not behind it. } ) 5... c6 { Holds d5 firmly and stops a White knight jumping to b5. } 6. e3 Be7 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. Qc2 O-O 9. Nge2 ( 9. Nf3 Re8 10. O-O Nf8 ) 9... Re8 { The rook takes the open file, and it frees d7 for the knight to leave. } 10. O-O Nf8 { The knight heads for g6 or e6 to guard the kingside and d5. } 11. h3 Ng6 { White will push b4-b5 to attack c6 (the minority attack). Black ignores it, plays ...Ne4 and ...Bd6, and aims at White's king instead. } *
